import { Node, html.div, html.h2, html.h3, html.p, html.strong } from "web";

export Node Manual() {
  return <div class="kc-panel kc-manual">
    <h2>Emergency field manual</h2>
    <p>Expert copy · R/V Nereid. Have the operator read the wet sensor, fault code, depth, floodwater and battery aloud.</p>
    <h3>01 / Isolate the leak</h3>
    <p>Close the bulkhead listed for the wet sensor. Closing a different bulkhead blocks the sump route and leaves the leak running.</p>
    <div class="kc-reading">BOW → B · MID → C · STERN → A</div>
    <h3>02 / Restore power and drain</h3>
    <p>Select the backup bus listed for the fault code. A wrong bus trips and costs 8% battery.</p>
    <div class="kc-reading">E1 → 3 · E2 → 1 · E3 → 2</div>
    <p>Switch the load to <strong>Pump</strong> once the leak is sealed and the bus is live. Pump and trim share one supply. Switch off the pump as soon as floodwater is at or below 25% to save battery.</p>
    <h3>03 / Surface</h3>
    <p>With the leak sealed, floodwater at or below 25%, and a working bus, switch the load to <strong>Trim</strong>, then <strong>Blow ballast</strong>. There is one air charge. Keep enough battery for ascent, which takes about one second per 14 m of depth.</p>
    <p>The boat is lost at 650 m, 100% floodwater, or 0% battery.</p>
  </div>;
}
